  "tagline": "ONE MISSING PIECE",
  "plannedCases": 12,
  "mainMystery": {
    "truth": "The new piece of Rome's ancient marble map was never lost. On Thursday night the builder Bruno Valli put a plaster copy in its glass case and took the real piece to his building site, because the piece shows an old Roman library under Piazza della Civetta, where his company will pour concrete for a car park. Restorer Livia Conti saw that the piece in the case was a copy. Nobody believed her, so she took the copy out on Friday at midnight and left owl cards to lead the detective to the proof.",
    "culprit": "Bruno Valli, the smiling sponsor of the museum's show and the owner of Valli Building.",
    "motive": "If people saw the library on the map, the city would stop his car park and he would lose a lot of money.",
    "revealCase": "s3_ep11"
  },
